{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAPjQu3Zws8nP3tsgtCx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `watch::Receiver::mark_unchanged`. Calling it makes the receiver treat the current value as already seen, so `has_changed()` returns `false` and `changed()` waits for the next send.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `tokio/src/sync/watch.rs`: the new method sits next to `mark_changed`. It sets the receiver's seen version to the channel's current version, the same way `has_changed` and `borrow_and_update` read it. It doesn't take the read lock or touch the closed flag.\n- `tokio/tests/sync_watch.rs`: a new `rx_mark_unchanged` test. It covers undoing `mark_changed`, ignoring a new `send`, and checks that `changed()` stays pending and the value is still readable.\n\n**Checks run:**\n- `cargo test --features full --test sync_watch`: 10 passed.\n- With the source change stashed, the new test fails to compile (`E0599: no method named mark_unchanged`).\n- `rustfmt --check` passes on both files, and the `sync::watch` doctests pass (18).\n- `clippy` shows only existing `unexpected_cfg(loom)` warnings from the newer toolchain, none from the new code.\n\n**Not done:** I didn't run the full tokio test suite or the loom tests, and I haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":357,"cache_read_input_tokens":38212,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":357,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82803cbb-4575-4ba1-8822-40af0834a937","uuid":"63e113d6-0e72-44c1-8d46-6c76b0082aed","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:13:24.628Z","request_id":"req_011CgAPjQgeYtmk3K1vC9XJo"}
